<title>CANADA: Canada Oct natural gas production rises 3.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada Oct natural gas production rises 3.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Friday issued the following data for crude oil and natural gas production and exports:</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL AND EQUIVALENT HYDROCARBONS (thousand cubic meters)</p>
<p>		    Oct 1996     Oct 1995	 pct</p>
<p>   Production  10,074.9	9,914.9	 +1.6</p>
<p>   Exports	5,688.4	5,237.3	 +8.6</p>
<p>   Imports	3,204.4	2,690.5	+19.1</p>
<p>   Ref receipts 7,894.4	7,133.0	+10.7</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (millions of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		   Oct 1996     Oct 1995	  pct</p>
<p>   Production  13,098.9     12,659.8	  3.5</p>
<p>   Exports	6,876.8	6,710.6	  2.5</p>
<p>   Canada sales 5,018.3	4,504.2	 11.4</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL (thousands of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		   Jan/Oct 1996  Jan/Oct 1995   pct</p>
<p>   Production     96,630.5   95,117.3	 1.6</p>
<p>   Exports	  53,076.4   50,568.9	 5.0</p>
<p>   Imports	  33,124.2   28,286.9	17.1</p>
<p>   Ref receipts   77,413.2   72,948.6	 6.1</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (milions of Cubic meters)</p>
<p>   Production    126,005.7  122,129.2	 3.2</p>
<p>   Exports	  66,245.3   65,350.3	 1.4</p>
<p>   Canada sales   52,667.9   49,904.3	 5.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Canada sales include direct sales.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact David Roeske, Energy Section, (613) 951-3563.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
